+/// Whether a parameter of type `ty` is the only path to the memory it
+/// points at while the call runs, which emit tells Zig with `noalias`
+/// (LLVM may then keep what it read there across a call that cannot
+/// reach that memory, such as a yield check's): a write view, held as
+/// a Zig pointer, of a value that does not change through a shared
+/// handle (`changesByMark`). A write lend is exclusive (Core §2): while
+/// it lasts no other loan, task, or handle reaches the value, so every
+/// access during the call goes through this pointer or one made from
+/// it. A Cell or Signal is written through any handle to it, so it is
+/// left out, as is a view whose type depends on a type parameter.
+pub fn exclusiveParam(ctx: *const SemContext, ty: TypeId) bool {
+    const inner = switch (ctx.types.get(ty)) {
+        .write_view => |inner| inner,
+        else => return false,
+    };
+    if (containsTypeVar(ctx, ty) or containsPoison(ctx, ty)) return false;
+    if (objectView(ctx, ty) != null or writeSliceElem(ctx, ty) != null) return false;
+    return !changesByMark(ctx, inner);
+}
